ohnson, Simon Joyner, Songs:Ohia. El neo-pop de Stephen Merritt (Magnetic Fields: Holiday, The Charm Of The Highway Strip, 69 Love Songs), Chris Connelly, Frank Black, Mike Gira (Body Lovers, Angels Of Light), Richard Davies y Eric Matthews (Cardinal), David Gray. El neo-folk de Beck (folk para la era del hip hop), John Frusciante, Sparklehorse, Bright Eyes, Rufus Wainwright, Grandaddy, Bobby Conn; el neo-country de Richard Buckner y Freedy Johnston; Steve Wynn, Mike Watt, Paul Westerberg, Ben Harper.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":128422149454877,"artist":"Ben Lee","artist_id":12223693612171,"title":"Breathing Tornados","year":1998,"ess":0,"yt":"UhyY1dZQvb0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores lo-fi de los noventa","scene_id":4419681145361,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.6"],"pages":[[1,249,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":249,"text":"…VAST, the project of San Francisco-based multi-instrumentalist Jon Crosby, epitomized unrelenting melodrama and symphonic arrangements. Australia's Ben Lee adopted a high-tech instrumentation of computers, keyboards, samplers and drum-machines on Breathing Tornados (1998). By borrowing ideas from…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":80026152013792,"type":"song","name":"Cigarettes Will Kill You","work_year":1998,"list_id":47661976793658,"list":"Triple J Hottest 100 · 1998","src":"singles","rank":2,"year":1998,"note":"Australia","yt":"F1WIBy6Imw8","scaruffi":null},{"id":222478615844328,"type":"song","name":"Nothing Much Happens","work_year":1999,"list_id":169477953497490,"list":"Triple J Hottest 100 · 1999","src":"singles","rank":81,"year":1999,"note":"A